{"id":"word:hebrew:H1141","type":"word","title":"בְּנָיָה","subtitle":"H1141 • Hebrew word","simple":{"meaning":"Benajah , the name of twelve Israelites","inThisVerse":"The selected word is tied to בְּנָיָה (H1141) in the Hebrew source text. Part of speech: n-pr-m.","whyItMatters":"This word appears 42 times in the Hebrew Bible, so BibleIQ can compare how Scripture uses it across multiple passages.","summary":"בְּנָיָה (Bᵉnâyâh) means Benajah , the name of twelve Israelites First listed occurrence: 1Chr 4 36."},"evidence":{"originalLanguage":{"source":"hebrew","word":"בְּנָיָה","transliteration":"Bᵉnâyâh","pronunciation":"ben-aw-yaw'","strong":"H1141","lemmaId":"hebrew:H1141","partOfSpeech":"n-pr-m","forms":["בְּנָיָ֧הוּ","בְּנָיָ֨הוּ֙","בְּנָיָ֖הוּ","וּ/בְנָיָ֨הוּ֙","וּ/בְנָיָֽה"],"morphs":[["HNp",23],["HC/Np",17],["HC/R/Np",2]]},"definitions":{"short":"Benajah , the name of twelve Israelites","usage":"Benaiah.","full":"H1141. Benayahu or Benayah בְּנָיָה בְּנָיָ֫הוּ, proper name, masculine ( Yah hath built up , compare יבנאל , Sabean בנאל DHM ZMG 1883, 15 ) — 1 one of David's captains and heroes, son of Jehoiada , בניהו 2Sam 8:18 ; 23:20 , 22 ; 1Kin 1:8 , 10 , 26 , 32 , 36 , 38 , 44 ; 2:25 , 29 , 30 (twice in verse); 2:34 ; 2:35 ; 2:46 ; 4:4 ; 1Chr 11:24 ; 18:17 ; 27:5-6 , compare 27:34 (see Be); = בניה 2Sam 20:23 ; 1Chr 11:22 . 2 one of David's thirty , בניהו 2Sam 23:30 = בניה 1Chr 11:31 ; 27:14 . 3 a Simeonite , בניה 1Chr 4:36 . 4 Levites , a. בניהו 1Chr 15:18 , 20 , 24 ; b. ( id. ) 2Chr 31:13 ; c. בניה 2Chr 20:14 . 5 Israelites , בניה a. Ezra 10:25 ; b. Ezra 10:30 ; c. Ezra 10:35 ; d. Ezra 10:43 ; e. Ezek 11:13 = בניהו 11:1 .","rootNote":"or בּנָיָהוּ ; (prolonged) from 1129 and 3050 ; Jah has built;","sources":["MorphHB occurrences","Strong Hebrew Dictionary","Brown-Driver-Briggs"]},"firstMention":"1Chr 4 36","keyReferences":["1Chr 4 36","1Chr 11 22","1Chr 11 24","1Chr 11 31","1Chr 15 18","1Chr 15 20","1Chr 15 24","1Chr 16 5"],"related":{"people":[],"places":[